    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Peat for the direct effects experiment was collected outside of the experimental SPRUCE units using a Russian corer. Samples were separated into 10-20 cm, 75-100 cm and 175-200 cm. For the indirect effects: soil quality, we collected peat from inside the experimental units at the same three depths. At the time of sample collection deep peat warming had been occurring for approximately 2 years. For both experiments, peat was frozen and shipped on ice to Chapman University for analysis. For the indirect effects: water table experiment, peat was collected along the depth profile and samples were immediately flushed to preserve anaerobic conditions. Unfrozen samples were shipped on ice to Chapman University for analysis. Please refer to Rush et al. (2021) for further site description, sampling and analysis details."
    ],
